    "result_text": "Full suite is green \u2014 35 tests, 0 failures, including the new `Cp25Tests`.\n\n## What I did\n\nAdded a 409-conflict check that rejects a new owner whose lower-cased email already belongs to another owner, following the existing telephone-uniqueness pattern in this OfficeFloor pipeline:\n\n1. **`CheckOwnerEmailUnique.java`** \u2014 new pipeline step. Reads the already-validated body via `@Val`, and if an email is present, compares it (lower-cased, trimmed) against every existing owner's email, throwing `OwnerEmailConflictException` on a match. Email is optional, so a request without one passes through.\n\n2. **`OwnerEmailConflictException.java`** \u2014 checked exception (`extends Exception`) so it surfaces as an escalation.\n\n3. **`OwnerEmailConflictExceptionHandler.java`** \u2014 responds `409 CONFLICT` with a `ProblemDetail`, mirroring the telephone handler.\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** \u2014 `...OwnerEmailConflictException.yml` wiring the exception to its handler.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `checkEmailUnique` step (under `transaction` governance) right after `checkTelephoneUnique` and before `checkHouseholdUnique`.\n\nThe request email is already normalized/lower-cased by the existing `ValidateOwnerFields` step, so the comparison catches differently-cased duplicates.",
